1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
Here is the augmented matrix of our system.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,250
Our goal is reduced row echelon form,

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,648
where the solution can simply be read off.

4
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:11,400
Picture it first.

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,733
Each equation is a line in the plane.

6
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:18,900
The solution is the single place where they all meet:

7
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,566
the point (1, 2).

8
00:00:20,566 --> 00:00:22,650
Row operations change the equations,

9
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,790
but never that meeting point.

10
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,016
Next,

11
00:00:27,016 --> 00:00:29,516
R₁ ↔ R₂,

12
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:34,568
to bring a nonzero entry into the pivot position of column 1.

13
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:35,900
Next,

14
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:40,483
R₂ → R₂ − 2R₁,

15
00:00:40,483 --> 00:00:44,723
which puts a zero below the pivot in column 1.

16
00:00:45,633 --> 00:00:48,550
Next, R₂ → (1/5)R₂.

17
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:52,716
Now the pivot in column 2 is a leading one.

18
00:00:52,716 --> 00:00:54,800
That completes the forward phase:

19
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,777
the matrix is in row echelon form.

20
00:00:58,683 --> 00:00:59,100
Next,

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,850
R₁ → R₁ + R₂,

22
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:07,491
which puts a zero above the leading one in column 2.

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:10,900
This is reduced row echelon form,

24
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,400
and the solution reads straight off:

25
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,368
x = 1, y = 2.

26
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:19,275
Let's check by putting these

27
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:21,566
values back into each original equation.

28
00:01:21,566 --> 00:01:25,383
Each of them holds, so the answer is right.

29
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:26,733
To recap:

30
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:28,400
get a leading one,

31
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,483
clear the entries below it,

32
00:01:30,483 --> 00:01:32,566
move to the next column,

33
00:01:32,566 --> 00:01:36,388
and finally clear the entries above each leading one.

34
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,566
Now it's your turn.

35
00:01:38,566 --> 00:01:41,483
Pause the video and solve this system.

36
00:01:41,483 --> 00:01:45,708
Your answer is checked in the write-up, so no peeking.

